---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site, url } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About" description={site.description}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <h1>About the club</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Placeholder: one or two sentences on why the club exists and who it is for.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we work on</h2>
      <p>
        Placeholder. Language models are trained, not programmed, so nobody writes down how they
        reach an answer. Interpretability is the work of finding out: locating the features and
        circuits inside a network and testing what they do. Safety asks what could go wrong as
        these systems become more capable, and what it takes to prevent it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we do</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Reading groups.</strong> Placeholder: we pick a paper, read it ahead of time, and
          work through it together.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Workshops.</strong> Placeholder: hands-on sessions with real models, such as
          probing activations, logit lens, and activation patching.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Talks.</strong> Placeholder: members and guests present research and projects.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Projects.</strong> Placeholder: small teams replicate a result or try a new idea
          over a semester.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who it is for</h2>
      <p>
        Placeholder. Any Georgia State student. Computer science, math, neuroscience, philosophy,
        and policy all have something to add. You do not need to have trained a model before.
      </p>

      <h2>People</h2>
      <p>Placeholder: officers and faculty advisor, with a line about each.</p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>, or see
        <a href={url('/join/')}>how to join</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
